Hello All,

>It's clear from Paul's original post, however, that there *is* some suspicion 
>of illegal activity.  

There is suspicion of what though?  It's a jump to assume that the
user is guilty of something.  The fact that a user has a 150
meg account where 5-20 meg is normal does not (by itself) indicate
criminal activity.  Taken alone this fact is shows only that the user
is taking up a great deal of space.  There is some 3rd hand rumor that
the user in question is doing 'wrong', but that's just rumor.  I
wonder if a magistrate would issue a search warrant based upon the
facts as we know them?

Interesting that we are all fairly clear on the rights of the user,
BUT we are not at all clear on the rights of the administrator to
protect his/her system from illegal activity.  The ECPA speaks to the
rights of administrators to (paraphrasing) do things that need to be
done to maintain the integrity of the system.  

-Rob-

