Subject:  An open letter to rap / Marie Coffin
Date: 2 May 1994 16:11:02 GMT
Message-ID: <2q38mm$mo0@hubcap.clemson.edu>


This is my last posting to rap.  I am leaving the newsgroup
immediately and permanently.  On Thursday, Barbara sent 30k of mail to
my sysadmin, complaining of my behavior to her and asking that my
account be yanked.  Barbara, of course, could not be aware of this, but
our network here is a small departmental one, which we administer
ourselves.  There was no chance that her allegations (some false, all
silly) would be taken seriously.  However, whenever Barbara chooses to
complain, my colleagues must read and deal with her mail.  To have a
madwoman brandishing an axe at me across the Internet is ugly and
embarrassing to all concerned, and does not put my department in a
good light.  Since there is no way of knowing when Barbara will next
erupt, or who will next be the recipient of her lies, I feel I have no
choice but to leave the newsgroup.  In fairness to my department, I
would like to emphasize that this is my own decision, and I have
received no pressure from my colleagues.

Barbara and I do not like each other, and until now I have chosen to
treat this as a personal problem which does not need to be aired.
Because I am leaving and because I am not the only person Barbara has
targeted, I am going to say some things that I would otherwise not
have said.  Barbara has been harrassing me off and on for months now.
Her first attempt to silence me was to call Marek at his office.  He
told her that he did not want to talk to her at work, and asked her to
please leave him alone.  She refused to do so, and repeated asked that
he 'make Marie stop picking on me'.  Since Marek and I have not dated
in over a year now, and have not seen each other in over a year, I do
not know how Barbara imagined that Marek could "make me" do anything.
The only explanation I can think of is ridiculously sexist: I cannot
believe Barbara meant that, so I can only say that I do not know what
she meant.

When that attempt failed, Barbara resorted to sending me e-mail,
saying that I had better "play nicey-nice" with her, or she would
reveal my secrets to the newsgroup.  I replied that I didn't want to
play anything with her, and that she didn't know any of my secrets.  

Now Barbara is trying to get my account yanked.  She will not succeed.
She will, however, succeed in silencing me.  One of her complaints to
my sysadmin was that I implied her poetry is terrible.  As a matter of
fact, I have never criticized Barbara's poetry at all, but she cannot
read well enough to realize that.  Oops, she doesn't like that remark
either.  However, whether the claim were true or not is irrevelant.  I
mention it because it shows what Barbara is trying to do.  She is
attempting, through threats and intimidation to have a kinder gentler
newsgroup where no one implies that her poetry is terrible, or
contradicts her opinions, or suggests that she is being irrational.  

So, Barbara, you can sleep easy tonight.  You need never worry again
that I will imply that your poetry is terrible, or that I will show
insufficient respect for your editing experience by saying that your
reading and grammar skills are lacking.  You can relax.  I'm sure it
will be a much "nicer" newsgroup without me.  But the rest of you, the
ones who subscribed to rec.arts.poems not knowing that it is being
forcibly changed to alt.fan.barbara, you may not sleep so well
tonight.  To those of you whom Barbara is also harrassing, who may be
in more vulnerable positions than I am, I can only offer my complete
sympathy, and my sincere hopes that she fails.

I have been an avid reader and poster to rap for over two
years now.  This has been my outlet for poetry, the place I could
count on getting honest criticism.  I will greatly miss this.  It is
hard for me to imagine how I will write poetry without it.  I thank
the many readers who have offered constructive criticism, and the many
writers who have given me joy by their poems.  You are too many to
mention by name, but I shall miss you all.  This used to be a great
place. 


Marie Coffin
