person again.  If that person persists, then you must do whatever you 
feel comfortable with.  

I do not believe that yanking someone's account or threatening to do so 
is an acceptable option if they are particularly disparaging about your 
poetry or just arbitrarily flame you.  Because posting poetry is a 
risky proposition, i.e., someone can tell you that you are great or 
that you suck shit, you are responsible ultimately because you posted 
it.  If you don't like or otherwise disagree with what someone said, you
may post an appropriate reply -- as is your right to do so.  If someone is
just
flaming you, you may ignore it or accept the bait -- your choice.  

There will always be someone that says something shitty.  With shit, there 
are two options, either fling it back, or plant flowers in it.

I prefer planting flowers to flinging shit, but that's my choice.

I also feel very strongly that we would be compromising the titillations of
our respective Muses, if this group became moderated or split up.  We would
be subject to (and thus our poetry  and criticism would be)
the whims of the moderator's interpretation of whatever rules
were concocted.  I feel that part of poetry is the fight and squabble over 
words, something that does go on in here a lot.  I don't like all of what
is said, but I am willing to tolerate and filter out what I see as crap. I
think anything else is oppressive at best.

I am sorry that you feel you have had a bad experience.  I would not treat
you like that, but that's me.   

