PRIVACY ISSUES

Just as there's nothing stopping the phone company from 
listening in on your conversations, people with system 
privileges have the power to examine all the mail that passes 
through "their" systems.  In practice, most system 
administrators are:
  a. honest and
  b. far to busy to read your mail, although there are 
infrequent occasions when they may inadvertently see private 
mail in the course of their system administration duties.  If 
the possibility of this happening bothers you, you should not 
use e-mail.  

ACNS reserves the right to take whatever steps are necessary 
to investigate security threats or violations of ACNS 
guidelines or University regulations.  On rare occasions, and 
with the approval of the Director or Associate Director, 
files belonging to private individuals may be examined.  

