too Dr. Fun I hardly think they are illegal. If offensive, then alot less
then the more perverse MAD style comics than is popular among lots of 
young boys.

In an earlier discussion on this newsgroup about censorship, at least one
example of illegal information was mentioned. This was concerning pictures 
of child sex (there is probably a nice word for that which I can't remember?).

I believe pictures of that would be illegal, and any University would be 
forced to remove such information quite quickly. URLs to such materials
might be a difficult legal issue, but I feel pretty sure that no University
here would take the time to find out since the objections to it would
probaly be quite loud anyway.

In my opinion, the problem is probably not so much concerning what is illegal
or not, but how much noise that would be generated if someone told them that 
students at Norwegian universities (which are completely financed by the state
and thus by the tax payers) transferred for instance pictures of Playboy 
bunnies for an estimated amount of $$$$$ (probably a rather large amount of 
money). Not to mention if some said that it would cost $$$$ (another large
number) less if the state just bought some magazines to the students instead.

Now... I feel I hear some arguments about cost and unused lines etc. 
But that is another issue and I think I'll rather go and eat a pizza (not 
to mention that I'm late with some school work already.. :(), than use a 
lot of time writing about it here...

Let there be freedom, alright for me.... as long as it is your money...

