But what about legal stuff?

We can define three types of the expressive material:
   1. Illegal (for example: libel, child porn, illegal porn)
   2. Legal, but not what the university would officially endorse
        (for example, some Dr. Fun cartoons, criticism of university policy,
           criticism of government policy, references to the United States
           as "AmeriKKKa")
    3. Legal material that the university would endorse

I think it is reasonable for the university to prohibit illegal (Type 1)
material. (Although, I don't think it should be held liable for
illegal material on its system that it doesn't know about.)

What I don't think is reasonable is for the university to prohibit
legal material that it would not officially endorse (Type 1 material).

Such a prohibition would make the students and professors mere puppets
of the the university and the government.

