>users who become major nuisances.That's  not just a right; it's 
>part of the administrator's JOB.
[...]

Here are U. of Illinois, not even professors have authority to
summarily expel students from class. They used to this authority (in
1904), but the authority was withdrawn.

Of course, in an emergency university staff have quite a bit of
authority to take reasonable measures to keep the university up and
running and to mitigate damage. But as far as punishing a student for
intermittently posting commerical articles to Usenet, I don't think
any university sys admin should have such authority. At a state
university, from many types of accounts, such authority would
probably be unconstitutional.

- Carl

